ert ratings consensus at Lean R"], "rationale": "Recent polls show a genuinely tight race, with several surveys putting Hinojosa within a point or two and a couple showing her narrowly ahead, but Abbott's incumbency, fundraising dominance, and Texas's Republican lean still favor him. Markets and most raters agree the race is Lean R despite the narrow polling margin.", "watch": "Whether national and outside Democratic spending materializes for Hinojosa could keep the race at the tossup edge the polls suggest.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Incumbent Greg Abbott (R) is running."]}, "overview": "Texas governor is closer than usual this cycle. Incumbent Greg Abbott seeks a third term against state Representative Gina Hinojosa, and recent polls show a narrow contest, with averages placing Abbott up only about one to two points. Some surveys, including a large YouGov poll and a New York Times/Siena poll, even show Hinojosa slightly ahead.\n\nStill, Abbott holds major structural advantages: he has raised over $25 million and retains $67 million on hand, far outstripping Hinojosa's $3 million, and no third-party candidate is a factor. Expert raters mostly call the race Lean R, and prediction markets give Abbott roughly a 75-79% chance. The race sits between the tight polls and the fundamentals, landing as a modest but real Republican edge.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.1819, "margin": -4.27}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.2694, "margin": -3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.2894, "margin": -3.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.2702, "margin": -3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.2293, "margin": -3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.2331, "margin": -3.3}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.2978, "margin": -3.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.2717, "margin": -3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.2616, "margin": -3.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.2625, "margin": -3.5}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.2248, "margin": -4.0}